  body: "# Criminal and civil custody boundary in chapter 12\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nFor the
    chapter’s general disqualification guidance, detention in legal custody is connected with criminal
    proceedings or imprisonment ordered by a criminal court; imprisonment in civil proceedings is expressly
    distinguished.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 12027 is a scoped meaning, not a universal definition
    of custody or a determination for a detained person. State Pension, mental-health detention, young
    offenders, remand and overseas detention have additional source provisions; benefits routed to other
    chapters or ADM require their own tests.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 12027, PDF page
    8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/651bcf2e6dfda6000d8e39d2/dmgch12.pdf#page=8) — DMG
    Vol 3 Ch 12: Imprisonment.\n- [DMG 12015, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/651bcf2e6dfda6000d8e39d2/dmgch12.pdf#page=3)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 12: Imprisonment.\n- [DMG 12016, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/651bcf2e6dfda6000d8e39d2/dmgch12.pdf#page=3)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 12: Imprisonment.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch12`: PDF SHA-256 `be79f9d6f8baf23290b8d6af5f384d31c2435b960fe3a59c14febd510fbaa9fe`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `989a5b292ba1f6129362ddc7ee736133798156d58c3539be2d0232fad5c92660`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/common-imprisonment-payability
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The kind of custody is an input to the chapter’s disqualification-from-payment
      question, whose effect is distinguished from entitlement.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0008
      quote: "12027 The term “imprisonment or detention in legal custody” means\n\n\n1. any detention
        connected with criminal proceedings1or\n\n\n2. imprisonment imposed by a criminal court2.\n\n\n\
        A claimant sentenced to imprisonment as a result of civil proceedings is not disqualified 2.\n\
        \n\n                                                                                       1 R(P)
        2/57; 2 R(S) 8/79"
      locator: DMG 12027
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0003
      quote: "12003 Claimants are disqualified from receiving these benefits when they are imprisoned
        or detained in\n\nlegal custody following criminal proceedings 1. Disqualification only affects
        the payability of the benefit\n\nnot claimants’ entitlement to that benefit2. This means that
        when the conditions supporting the\ndisqualification no longer apply, payment of benefit can resume
        providing all the conditions of\nentitlement remain satisfied. Unless entitlement has been terminated
        during the period of imprisonment\nor detention in legal custody, a claimant should not be required
        to make a new claim to benefit on\nrelease.\n\n\n                                            \
        \                   1 SS CB Act 92, s 113(1)(b); 2 CDLA/1930/04\n\n\n12004 - 12014\n\n\n\nEffect
        of imprisonment on JSA, IS, SPC and ESA"
      locator: DMG 12003
